# Silver Sable, Mercenary Leader: "target modified creature you control" is checked again as the attack trigger resolves (CR 608.2b,
# 700.9). Bot1's Ornithopter, enchanted by Bot1's Rancor, is the one modified creature Bot1 controls when Sable attacks, so the trigger
# targets it; Bot2 answers with Disenchant on Rancor. The Ornithopter is no longer modified, so it is an illegal target and the trigger
# does nothing: no lifelink. (The positive control is silver-sable-a-creature-enchanted-by-your-aura-is-modified-and-gains-lifelink.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Silver Sable, Mercenary Leader
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Ornithopter
Rancor
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Disenchant
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Rancor.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Silver Sable, Mercenary Leader.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Silver Sable, Mercenary Leader > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Disenchant.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Rancor)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying
Bot2.Graveyard = Disenchant
